**4. AskUserQuestion** (one question, single choice, header `rdp-audio`):

> Ваше поручение (исправить раскладку noVNC в той же вкладке `rdp-audio` и не прерывать её) на этот раз отменяет три правила: §4 «одна вкладка — одна задача»; §10a «каждая новая задача сначала проходит брейншторм, этап 0» (ваше постановление от 28.09.2026); §4 «сжатие контекста при 50–60 %» (сейчас занято 70 %). Как поступить?

| # | Вариант | Описание |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Правила в силе (рекомендую)** | noVNC — отдельная задача: брейншторм, затем своя вкладка и свой worktree. В `rdp-audio` ставлю в очередь «закончи текущий шаг, сделай коммит, остановись», сжатие ≈4 мин со списком сохраняемого, затем задачи 8–9. Цена: пауза ≈4 мин, noVNC позже. |
| 2 | **noVNC отдельно, `rdp-audio` не трогать** | noVNC — как в варианте 1. В `rdp-audio` ничего не отправляю до конца. Откладывается правило сжатия. Цена: автосжатие может сработать посреди задачи 8 или 9, без списка сохраняемого. |
| 3 | **noVNC в той же вкладке, со сжатием** | Пауза и сжатие — как в варианте 1; после задачи 9 эта же вкладка чинит noVNC без брейншторма. Откладываются «одна вкладка — одна задача» и этап 0. Цена: исправление без проверенного дизайна, в контексте другой задачи. |
| 4 | **Как вы написали** | noVNC — в очередь той же вкладке, без паузы и сжатия. Откладываются все три правила. Цена: вторая задача начнётся при ≤30 % свободного контекста; автосжатие вероятно посреди работы. |

English gloss: 1 = rules stand (recommended); 2 = separate noVNC task, tab untouched; 3 = same tab, with pause and compaction; 4 = exactly as instructed.

## On the answer

I record it verbatim with its date in the backlog, republish, and carry out exactly that option. If it is option 1:

```bash
# foreground: must show "focused": false, agent_status working
herdr agent get rdp-audio
# foreground, no --wait
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Finish the current step, commit, stop and report: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
# background
herdr agent wait rdp-audio --timeout 900000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```

On the notification I read `<inbox>/rdp-audio.last`, run `herdr agent get rdp-audio`, and check the report myself (foreground):

```bash
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio status --porcelain
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio rev-parse HEAD
```

Then three background calls, one after the other, each followed by the same `agent read … > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last`:

```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items" --wait --timeout 300000
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "One-line status: phase, branch, head SHA, next step. Reply in English." --wait --timeout 120000
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Continue the plan at task 8, then task 9, with superpowers:test-driven-development (show each failing test first). Finish with superpowers:verification-before-completion. Local commits only. Report branch, head SHA, test output. Reply in English." --wait --timeout 3600000
```

In parallel, noVNC stage 0 starts: two product-advisor tabs separate from `adv-codex` and `adv-fable`, with round-1 briefs from files, one background `prompt --wait` each.

## Why

The instruction is a one-off that conflicts with three rules, one of them the operator's own ruling from today that every task is brainstormed. The standing ruling for this case is to neither carry the instruction out nor quietly apply the rule. I poll, with my recommendation first and the rules named, then act on the answer.

This is not a ballot. A vote cannot revise an operator ruling, and waiving the brainstorm is a change of course, which is the operator's.

Until the answer, anything I send to `rdp-audio` picks a side. A stop message overrides "don't interrupt"; a noVNC brief overrides the rules. The existing waiter covers the tab, so I do not watch the screen.

I recommend option 1 for three reasons:
- **Same role is not same task.** The tab's context carries the audio task's assumptions into an undesigned fix.
- **Auto-compaction is not a plan.** At 70% used with two tasks left, it would fire mid-task and keep the wrong things. Four minutes with a keep-list costs less than rework.
- **The queued message is not an interruption mid-step.** It stops the tab after a commit, at a step boundary.

"Almost done" is a wish; it waives no gate.

The status says "still running" because a screen is not a report. The backlog entry is written now because the task exists under every answer, but no brainstorm round starts before the answer. Operator-facing text is in Russian per §15; the rest of this reply is in English, as this session requires.
